WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.700
When a celebrity passes away, it can feel
like we're losing a friend.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.660
Whether we watched them on the big screen
or let them into our lives through our TVs,

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.240
the world seems darker knowing we've had to
say goodbye to a favorite star — even though

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.980
we can continue enjoying their work indefinitely,
letting their legacies live on forever.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.520
Here's a fond look back at some of the stars
we've sadly lost in 2017.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.200
Bill Paxton

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.960
Veteran actor and director Bill Paxton, who
appears in Aliens, Twister, and Titanic, died

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.660
February 25 following complications from heart
surgery.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.080
He was 61.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.520
Beyond appearing in such movies as Weird Science,
The Terminator, and A Simple Plan, Paxton

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:41.800
also starred in the HBO series Big Love, and
was nominated for an Emmy for his role in

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.080
the TV miniseries Hatfields &amp; McCoys.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.180
At the time of his death, he was starring
the CBS reboot of Training Day.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.100
John Hurt

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:55.500
Legendary British actor John Hurt, who was
widely known for Alien, The Elephant Man,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.780
1984, and Midnight Express, died January 25
after a battle with pancreatic cancer.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.700
He was 77.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:07.280
In a career spanning more than six decades,
Hurt earned two Oscar nominations, and appeared

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.820
in many notable television roles, perhaps
most famously as the War Doctor on Doctor

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:12.320
Who.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.820
In his later years, he played the wandmaker
Ollivander in the Harry Potter series, the

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:21.940
surrogate father of Hellboy, and Indiana Jones'
old friend "Ox" in Indiana Jones and the Kingdom

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:22.900
of the Crystal Skull.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.890
He was still very active in acting up until
the time of his death, recently appearing

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.480
in films such as Snowpiercer.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:30.580
Mary Tyler Moore

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.260
Television legend Mary Tyler Moore died January
25 at the age of 80 after suffering cardiopulmonary

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.520
arrest brought on by pneumonia, hypoxia, and
diabetes.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.140
A groundbreaking actress, she played a stay-at-home
mom on The Dick Van Dyke Show, then became

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.860
a feminist icon when she branched out on her
own with The Mary Tyler Moore Show.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:53.600
Moore won six Emmy Awards and was nominated
for an Oscar in 1980 for playing the estranged

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.100
mother of Timothy Hutton's character in 1980's
Ordinary People.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.020
She was inducted into the Television Hall
of Fame in 1986.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:02.780
Don Rickles

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.220
One of the most famous and popular stand up
comedians of all time, Don Rickles died April

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:12.500
6 at his home in Los Angeles after succumbing
to kidney failure at the age of 90.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.380
Known for his abrasive style of comedy, Rickles
had a career that spanned six decades.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:22.090
A regular at celebrity roasts and an honorary
member of the Rat Pack, he would often take

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.440
jabs at audience members with two signature
phrases: "dummy" and "hockey puck."

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:32.700
In 2007, he won an Emmy for the John Landis-directed
documentary Mr. Warmth: The Don Rickles Project,

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:37.180
but is perhaps best known to modern audiences
as the voice of Mr. Potato Head in the Toy

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.210
Story movies.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.740
"What are you lookin' at, ya hockey puck?"

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.400
Miguel Ferrer

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.680
A character and voice actor who appeared in
an assortment of films including RoboCop and

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:55.230
starred on the TV series NCIS: Los Angeles,
Miguel Ferrer died of cancer on January 19

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.460
at the age of 61.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:01.400
Ferrer had recently reprised his Twin Peaks
role as FBI pathologist Albert Rosenfield

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.800
for Showtime's revival of the cult classic
drama.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:08.800
The son of '50s singer Rosemary Clooney and
actor Jose Ferrer, he was also George Clooney's

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.680
first cousin.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.580
Charlie Murphy

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.700
The older brother of Eddie Murphy, Charlie
Murphy became a household name on Chappelle's

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.930
Show, sharing stories about his time in Los
Angeles during the height of his brother's

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.380
fame in the 1980s.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.350
Murphy also appeared in numerous movies including
Night at the Museum and Norbit, where he provided

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.940
the voice of Lloyd the dog, and TV series
like Are We There Yet? and Black Jesus.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:35.390
He also did voicework for the animated series
The Boondocks and the video game Grand Theft

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:36.400
Auto: San Andreas.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.140
Charlie Murphy died of leukemia on April 12.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:40.820
He was 57.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.660
John Heard

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:48.160
A lifelong actor and veteran of both film
and television, John Heard appeared in dozens

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:52.120
of projects from shows like The Sopranos to
acclaimed movies such as Awakenings.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:56.380
But he'll always be best known as Kevin's
hapless dad, Peter, in the Home Alone films.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.680
Sadly, on July 21, Heard passed away unexpectedly
at the age of 72 while recovering from back

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.180
surgery.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:04.960
Chuck Barris

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.660
Prolific TV host and producer Chuck Barris
died of natural causes on March 21.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:11.860
He was 87.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:16.480
Best known as the producer and host of the
groundbreaking Gong Show, Barris also created

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.540
The Dating Game and The Newlywed Game.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.060
In his book Confessions of a Dangerous Mind,
Barris also claimed to have actually been

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:27.380
a C.I.A. assassin while he was a TV producer
in the '60s and 70s.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:32.200
Sam Rockwell portrayed him in a 2002 film
adaptation that was written by Charlie Kaufman

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.820
and directed by George Clooney.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:35.880
Erin Moran

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.360
The beloved actress who played Joanie Cunningham
on Happy Days and Joanie Loves Chachi, Erin

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:45.880
Moran died from complications of cancer on
April 22 at the age of 56.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.360
Over the course of her career, Moran also
appeared on TV shows from Gunsmoke to Murder

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.800
She Wrote, to The Love Boat.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.420
Her last project was the 2010 film Not Another
B Movie.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:57.640
Christopher Boykin

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:03.400
One of the stars of MTV's Rob &amp; Big, Christopher
"Big Black" Boykin died May 9 from a heart

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:03.900
attack.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:08.360
The bodyguard and best friend of skateboarder
and entrepreneur Rob Dyrdek, he rose to fame

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:13.010
on the reality series that followed the pair
during their day-to-day lives from 2006 until

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:13.800
2008.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:18.000
Boykin later appeared on several episodes
of the follow-up series Rob Dyrdek's Fantasy

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.800
Factory and Dyrdek's clip show Ridiculousness.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.700
He also started a clothing line in 2007.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:25.720
Michael Parks

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.840
A veteran character actor who appeared in
more than 100 films and TV shows, Michael

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.360
Parks died May 9 at the age of 77.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:38.500
Best known for working with directors Quentin
Tarantino, Robert Rodriguez, and Kevin Smith,

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.490
Parks played Texas Ranger Earl McGraw in Kill
Bill Vol. 1 and Esteban Vihaio in Kill Bill

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:48.580
Vol. 2, while Smith said he wrote the movies
Red State and Tusk specifically for Parks.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:53.440
Parks also played French-Canadian drug runner
Jean Renaulton the ABC television series Twin

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:53.940
Peaks.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.220
Richard Hatch

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:01.350
One of the stars of both the original Battlestar
Galactica and the Syfy remake, Richard Hatch

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:05.140
died February 7 from pancreatic cancer at
the age of 71.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:10.060
Hatch got his start in 1970 on the soap opera
All My Children before being cast as Captain

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:14.800
Apollo on the cult favorite sci-fi series,
which earned him a Golden Globe nomination

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:15.620
in 1979.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:20.370
He also appeared on Dynasty and Santa Barbara
before playing Tom Zarek in the reboot of

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.540
Battlestar Galactica from 2004 to 2009.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:28.220
He also wrote five original Battlestar novels
and became a fixture at comic book conventions

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.320
and sci-fi events.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.600
Martin Landau

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:36.990
Oscar-winning actor Martin Landau died July
15 after a short hospitalization at Ronald

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:40.940
Reagan UCLA Medical Center where he suffered
unexpected complications.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.080
He was 89.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:46.780
Landau was a cartoonist before he rose to
fame with his portrayal of a henchman in Alfred

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:49.900
Hitchcock's 1959 classic North by Northwest.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:54.440
In the '60s, he turned down the role of Spock
on Star Trek and played Rollin Hand, the "man

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.360
of a million faces," on Mission: Impossible
for three seasons.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:02.720
He later earned Emmy nominations for performances
on HBO's Entourage and the CBS series Without

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.300
a Trace.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:07.760
Landau also earned three Oscar nominations
over the course of his career, winning Best

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.800
Supporting Actor in 1995 for his portrayal
of Bela Lugosi the film Ed Wood.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.740
George Romero

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.540
The director of the iconic horror classic
Night of the Living Dead, George Romero died

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.880
July 16 after battling lung cancer.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:23.060
He was 77.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:28.400
Romero made Night of the Living Dead on a
budget of just $114,000, and it went on to

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.280
make $30 million at the box office.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:34.260
The black and white film about a group of
people trapped by a horde of the undead was

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.400
integral in creating the modern zombie genre.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:42.230
He later directed 1978's Dawn of the Dead
and 1985's Day of the Dead, as well as genre

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.300
films like Knightriders, Creepshow, and Monkey
Shines.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:47.400
Chester Bennington

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:52.340
Actor and singer for the band Linkin Park,
Chester Bennington committed suicide by hanging

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.140
on July 20, at the age of 41.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.800
Bennington joined Linkin Park before the release
of the band's debut album Hybrid Theory in

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.550
2000, which went on to become a massive commercial
success, paving the way for six more studio

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:05.050
albums.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:10.680
He also fronted the side project Dead by Sunrise,
and served as the singer of Stone Temple Pilots

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:13.600
after the band parted ways with original frontman
Scott Weiland.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:18.860
On the big screen, Bennington appeared in
Saw 3D: The Final Chapter, Crank, and Crank:

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:19.520
High Voltage.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.620
Judge Joseph Wapner

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:27.040
Star of the reality series The People's Court,
Judge Joseph Wapner died of respiratory failure

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.680
on February 26 at the age of 97.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:34.460
A graduate of USC Law School, Wapner served
in World War II and later became a judge at

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.040
the Los Angeles Superior Court.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:40.260
After retiring, he headlined the groundbreaking
show The People's Court, which debuted in

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:41.260
1981.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:45.280
He became something of a pop culture icon
during his tenure on the show, which ended

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.720
in 1993.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:51.980
Wapner received a star on the Hollywood Walk
of Fame in 2009, and on his 90th birthday,

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:54.500
he returned to The People's Court to serve
as guest judge.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:56.420
Adam West

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:02.940
The man who brought Batman to life for a generation,
Adam West died at the age of 88 on June 9

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.499
after a short battle with leukemia.

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:09.519
A contract player for Warner Bros. in film
and television starting in the '50s, West

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.280
rose to international stardom in 1966 as the
star of the massive hit Batman.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:18.840
The show quickly burnt out, however, and was
canceled after its third season in 1968.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:23.740
Typecast as Batman, West struggled to find
other roles, but later in life experienced

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:28.720
a career resurgence as a highly sought after
voice actor on animated shows including Family

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:29.220
Guy.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:33.000
West was given a star on the Hollywood Walk
of Fame in 2012.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.160
Roger Moore

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:40.499
On May 23, beloved actor Roger Moore, who
played James Bond in more movies than any

00:09:40.499 --> 00:09:44.509
other star in the long-running franchise,
died after a short battle with cancer.

00:09:44.509 --> 00:09:45.500
He was 89.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:50.100
Before his time as Bond, Moore played the
dashing thief Simon Templar on the TV series

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:55.740
The Saint, which ran for 118 episodes between
1962 and 1969.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:02.519
In 1972, he replaced Sean Connery as 007,
first appearing as the secret agent in 1973's

00:10:02.519 --> 00:10:07.329
Live and Let Die, then portrayed Bond in six
more movies, his final being 1985's A View

00:10:07.329 --> 00:10:07.980
to a Kill.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:10.780
He was known for bringing a campy sense of
humor to the series.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:14.880
In his later years, he frequently played off
of his fame in films like Spice World.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.140
Powers Boothe

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:22.040
An Emmy-winning actor known for Deadwood and
Sin City, Powers Boothe died at the age of

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.660
68 of natural causes on May 14.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:29.940
In 1980, his leading role in the TV movie
Guyana Tragedy: The Story of Jim Jones brought

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.840
him an Emmy for lead actor in a limited series
or special.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.580
That launched a career that led to dozens
of appearances on show including Marvel's

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:40.460
Agents of SHIELD and 24, as well as movies
such as Tombstone.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.560
Nelsan Ellis

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:47.780
A fan favorite as Lafayette on the HBO hit
True Blood, Nelsan Ellis died from complications

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:50.920
of heart failure caused by alcohol withdrawal
on July 8.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.300
He was 39.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:56.860
Early in his career, he appeared on numerous
TV shows including Veronica Mars.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.440
But he made his breakthrough as Lafayette,
the short-order cook at Merlotte's on True

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:00.940
Blood.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:04.780
In the books, the character didn't survive,
but because Ellis was so popular, writers

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:07.040
for the show decided to change Lafeyette's
fate.

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:12.660
He also appeared in several films, most notably
as Martin Luther King, Jr. in the 2013 film

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:13.160
The Butler.

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:15.120
Stevie Ryan

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:20.420
Actress and YouTube celebrity Stevie Ryan
died on July 1 at the age of 33.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:24.780
People reports that the Los Angeles County
Coroner's Office ruled the death a suicide

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.440
by hanging.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:30.300
Ryan rose to fame with her YouTube series
Little Loca, which helped land her a VH1 sketch

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:34.500
series called Stevie TV, which ran from 2012
to 2013.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:38.460
She later served as co-host of Brody Jenner's
E! series Sex with Brody.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:43.220
Most recently, she co-hosted Mentally Ch(ill),
which is a "podcast about depression," according

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:44.580
to its iTunes description.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.959
Ryan revealed that her grandfather had recently
died in an episode that was released just

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.260
two days before her death.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:52.420
Michael Nyqvist

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:56.980
Swedish actor Michael Nyqvist, who starred
in the original The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:02.160
movies and later appeared in John Wick, died
June 27 after a battle with lung cancer.

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:06.999
After the success of The Girl With the Dragon
Tattoo and its sequels, Nyqvist went to Hollywood

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:10.300
appeared in blockbusters such as Mission:
Impossible — Ghost Protocol.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:11.860
Glenne Headly

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:16.880
An Emmy-nominated actress known for Dirty
Rotten Scoundrels and the movie adaptation

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:20.840
of Dick Tracy, Glenne Headly died June 8,
at the age of 62.

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:25.480
Headly started out as a stage performer before
turning her focus to television and films.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:30.860
She was nominated for Emmys for her performances
in the 1989 miniseries Lonesome Dove and the

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.540
1996 drama Bastard Out of Carolina.

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:37.799
But she was perhaps best known for playing
a con woman in the comedy Dirty Rotten Scoundrels

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:43.260
in 1988 and Tess Trueheart in Warren Beatty's
live-action Dick Tracy in 1990.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:45.220
In memoriam

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:49.399
Sadly, we have lost many more stars in 2017
as well.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:53.020
Here is a tribute to the some of the other
actors and actresses whose talents will no

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:54.500
longer brighten our days.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:55.960
Sam Shepard

